<Page title="About Lily Smith | Author, Brand Strategist and Educator" description="Meet Lily Smith, an author, brand strategist, educator, self-publishing guide, and mother helping creative experts build meaningful brands." active="About">
  <section class="about-hero shell">
    <div class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Meet Lily Smith</p><h1>Author, brand strategist,<br/><em>educator, and mom.</em></h1><p class="lede">I help authors and creative experts clarify their message, build a thoughtful online presence, and share what they know with confidence.</p></div>
    <div class="portrait about-portrait" role="img" aria-label="Lavender portrait placeholder for Lily Smith"><div class="sun"></div><div class="arch"></div><div class="initials">LS</div><p>A creative business<br/>built for real life</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="subsection"><div class="shell copy-grid"><h2>A brand education business built around real life.</h2><div><p>I began in brand development, helping small businesses and creative professionals find the words and direction that made their work easier to understand.</p><p>After becoming a mother, I wanted a different kind of business. One with thoughtful systems, room for family, and a definition of success that still felt human.</p><p>Today I teach brand strategy, social media planning, and self-publishing through coaching, workshops, and practical resources.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="personal shell"><div class="personal-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Beyond the professional bio</p><h2>A little more<br/><em>about me.</em></h2><p>Most days, you will find me working at the kitchen table with a cup of tea nearby and at least one forgotten load of laundry upstairs.</p></div><div class="personal-notes"><p>Tuesday tacos are our family’s most reliable tradition. We add extra lime, keep the salsa mild for the kids, and avoid complicated recipes.</p><p>In the backyard, I grow herbs, tomatoes, and more lavender than I know what to do with. Gardening reminds me that good things take their own time.</p><p>There are books in every room: memoirs on the nightstand, cookbooks in the kitchen, and picture books tucked into nearly every basket.</p><p>My favorite weekends begin slowly, with pancakes, music in the kitchen, and a family walk before anyone starts thinking about the week ahead.</p></div></section>
</Page>
